WEBVTT

00:00:03.750 --> 00:00:04.600
You have one new message

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:07.420
You have one new message

00:00:08.150 --> 00:00:11.610
<b>Forward World</b>

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.870
Arima Ichika

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.870
Arima Ichika

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.870
Good evening.
Do you have some time after
school tomorrow?

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:15.870
Who says "good evening"?

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.490
<b>Forward World</b>

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.500
I have plans tomorrow.
Can we meet up on Saturday?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Arima Ichika

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:24.500
Good evening.
Do you have some time after
school tomorrow?

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.130
Saturday...

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.010
Tamaru-kun

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.010
Good evening.
Do you have some time after
school tomorrow?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.010
Tamaru-kun

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.010
I have plans tomorrow.
Can we meet up on Saturday?

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:32.010
Does meeting in front of the 
station at 1 PM work for you?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.510
Good evening.
Do you have some time after
school tomorrow?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.510
Tamaru-kun

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.510
I have plans tomorrow. 
Can we meet up on Saturday?

00:00:33.510 --> 00:00:36.510
Does meeting in front of the 
station at 1 PM work for you?

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:36.510
Tamaru-kun

00:00:35.530 --> 00:00:36.510
Sure thing.

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:45.760
Tamaru-kun!

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:48.820
Sorry! Have you been waiting long?

00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:50.220
No, not at all.

00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:53.530
So, hey.

00:00:54.410 --> 00:00:56.230
About my reply...

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:56.950
Huh?!

00:00:56.950 --> 00:01:00.100
Arima, hang on a second. Are you 
seriously going to tell me here?

00:01:05.310 --> 00:01:08.680
R-Right. I guess I panicked.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:11.550
Let's go somewhere else.

00:01:12.270 --> 00:01:13.420
Yeah.

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:28.860
Arima, your ice cream's melting.

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:30.390
Oh, you're right.

00:01:30.390 --> 00:01:31.770
I'm done with mine.

00:01:33.190 --> 00:01:36.330
This is my first time having ice cream 
from here. It's really good.

00:01:37.790 --> 00:01:40.660
So... could you give me your reply?

00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:45.450
Yeah.

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:51.460
Tamaru-kun...

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:55.910
You're really cool, and kind, 
and we have a lot in common.

00:01:55.910 --> 00:01:58.570
I think it'd be really 
fun to go out with you.

00:01:59.450 --> 00:02:00.180
Thanks...

00:02:01.630 --> 00:02:04.890
I was really happy... that you asked me out.

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:06.140
But...

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.570
There's someone else that I like.

00:02:10.430 --> 00:02:11.400
So...

00:02:11.790 --> 00:02:15.730
I can't go out with you.

00:02:18.990 --> 00:02:23.240
What if I asked you to go out with me
even if you like someone else?

00:02:23.240 --> 00:02:24.110
Huh?

00:02:24.940 --> 00:02:28.500
I-I can't... do that.

00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:33.920
Yeah, I figured.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.060
It's true that I really 
enjoy our time together...

00:02:41.660 --> 00:02:44.900
And I want you to continue being my friend.

00:02:47.540 --> 00:02:50.330
I'm sorry. I know that's really selfish.

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:58.030
It'd be worse if you avoided me from now on.

00:03:02.520 --> 00:03:04.690
I'll lend you some more books soon.

00:03:05.930 --> 00:03:07.790
Let me know what you think about them.

00:03:09.310 --> 00:03:10.490
Thanks.

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:17.220
So, hey. Can I be a little selfish, too?

00:03:17.220 --> 00:03:18.760
Huh? Sure.

00:03:19.860 --> 00:03:23.500
Do you mind if I stay in love with you?

00:03:24.790 --> 00:03:29.110
Until I can sort out my 
feelings... Is that okay?

00:03:32.170 --> 00:03:34.770
Sure, okay.

00:03:36.650 --> 00:03:37.520
Good.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:43.120
By the way, your ice cream 
is basically just goo now.

00:03:43.120 --> 00:03:44.740
Oh, y-you're right!

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:51.040
I'll walk you to the gates.

00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:52.460
Thanks.

00:03:53.290 --> 00:03:57.880
But when you downed the 
ice cream soup back there...

00:03:58.170 --> 00:04:00.880
That was pretty manly and impressive.

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:03.580
Ugh, I'm just going to drink all this.

00:04:03.900 --> 00:04:05.950
<b>G
u
u
u
l
p</b>

00:04:04.430 --> 00:04:05.390
Did you just down it?

00:04:05.390 --> 00:04:08.170
Well, what else was I supposed to do with it?

00:04:08.170 --> 00:04:11.480
Well, you just went for it harder 
than I thought you would.

00:04:12.690 --> 00:04:14.880
So much so that you're laughing at me?

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:15.950
Ichika-san...

00:04:20.560 --> 00:04:21.580
Ryo-san.

00:04:24.220 --> 00:04:27.490
I'll head back to the office 
first and get that report done.

00:04:27.490 --> 00:04:29.770
Uh, right. Thanks.

00:04:33.220 --> 00:04:34.330
Anyway...

00:04:36.050 --> 00:04:37.500
Hello, you two.

00:04:38.590 --> 00:04:42.210
So... are you on a date?

00:04:41.280 --> 00:04:42.210
<b>Smile</b>

00:04:42.430 --> 00:04:44.810
<i>His face and his aura are 
contradicting each other.</i>

00:04:47.930 --> 00:04:49.670
Um, this is...

00:04:51.740 --> 00:04:56.370
Then I guess you're going to end 
up being my brother's rival.

00:04:57.420 --> 00:04:58.360
<i>Yeah, I will.</i>

00:05:00.490 --> 00:05:03.210
Um, don't get the wrong idea.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:06.950
Arima just rejected me.

00:05:07.510 --> 00:05:09.150
T-Tamaru-kun...

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:10.920
She rejected you?

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:16.170
I don't know what you're 
hiding behind that smile,

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:19.140
nor do I really want to know,

00:05:19.480 --> 00:05:23.880
but just make sure you don't 
do anything to make Arima sad.

00:05:25.370 --> 00:05:27.600
Well, aren't you all high and mighty?

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:30.230
I think it's even more immature 
for you to try to use

00:05:30.230 --> 00:05:31.930
the fact that you're older against me.

00:05:34.440 --> 00:05:35.560
Yeah, you're right.

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:37.260
Thanks for the heads-up.

00:05:38.780 --> 00:05:41.650
<i>I think I just caught a 
glimpse of who he really is.</i>

00:05:41.650 --> 00:05:44.840
Hey, Arima. Do you mind if I take off now?

00:05:44.840 --> 00:05:48.160
S-Sure, that's fine. Tamaru-kun...

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:50.690
Thank you for everything today.

00:05:51.610 --> 00:05:53.130
I'll see you at school.

00:05:56.300 --> 00:05:59.120
Er... Can I ask what's going on?

00:06:01.530 --> 00:06:05.610
Tamaru-kun asked me out the other day,

00:06:05.610 --> 00:06:08.630
and I met with him today 
to give him my answer.

00:06:09.640 --> 00:06:12.280
Wait... Is this what you were troubled over?

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:16.600
This is a problem that I need 
to figure out on my own...

00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.340
Yes.

00:06:18.820 --> 00:06:20.600
I see.

00:06:20.830 --> 00:06:25.650
Wait, you declined? Does that mean you—

00:06:30.420 --> 00:06:31.810
<i>How stupid am I?</i>

00:06:33.650 --> 00:06:34.710
<i>I'm so immature.</i>

00:06:36.310 --> 00:06:38.190
Hello? Kawaguchi?

00:06:39.390 --> 00:06:44.390
I know this is sudden, but I wanted to keep 
my promise from the ball game tournament.

00:06:45.510 --> 00:06:47.380
I told you that I'd tell you.

00:06:48.750 --> 00:06:51.420
I asked Arima out.

00:06:51.420 --> 00:06:54.380
And I'm on my way home now 
because she turned me down.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:07:00.020
Huh? You want to cheer me up? Yeah, no.

00:07:00.470 --> 00:07:01.520
Yamagishi's coming, too?

00:07:02.260 --> 00:07:03.870
Give me a break, guys.

00:07:12.520 --> 00:07:16.020
<i>I've never seen Ichika-san 
make a face like that.</i>

00:07:16.740 --> 00:07:19.290
I think it's even more 
immature for you to try

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:21.330
to use the fact that you're older against me.

00:07:21.330 --> 00:07:23.460
<i>Oh, I see.</i>

00:07:24.720 --> 00:07:28.470
<i>I'm frustrated because 
it wasn't because of me.</i>

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:58.970
Koikimo

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.980
Episode 9

00:08:58.970 --> 00:09:03.980
"My Answer"

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:16.950
<b>Graduation Day
Congratulations,
Everyone</b>

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:20.190
Hey, Tamaru, why'd you write 
"Graduation Day" so small?

00:09:20.190 --> 00:09:23.560
I didn't. Your "Congratulations" 
is just way too big.

00:09:23.560 --> 00:09:27.330
What? How else are all the farsighted 
people supposed to read it, then?

00:09:27.330 --> 00:09:29.580
This size shows how much I care.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:32.010
I don't think any of the 
graduates are farsighted.

00:09:32.010 --> 00:09:34.090
Come on, you two...

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:37.430
20 minutes ago—

00:09:35.690 --> 00:09:37.430
Arima! Amakusa!

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:39.030
Perfect timing!

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:41.690
If you're free, help me out a bit.

00:09:41.690 --> 00:09:44.840
That'll all come down to what you 
want and what we get in return.

00:09:44.840 --> 00:09:46.160
I'll buy you some drinks.

00:09:46.160 --> 00:09:49.020
If what you need is equivalent 
to some drinks, sure.

00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:52.440
<i>Rio's negotiation skills 
never cease to amaze me.</i>

00:09:52.440 --> 00:09:55.190
Arima, you're in the art club, right?

00:09:55.190 --> 00:09:56.090
Yes.

00:09:56.090 --> 00:09:57.510
Then you're the perfect candidate.

00:09:58.350 --> 00:09:59.910
Oh, hey. Tamaru!

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.960
Perfect timing! Would you 
mind helping me out, too?

00:10:02.960 --> 00:10:04.860
The more the merrier.

00:10:06.210 --> 00:10:07.910
Tomorrow's graduation, right?

00:10:07.910 --> 00:10:12.680
Could you write some kind of message 
in their classrooms to send them off?

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:15.920
Draw a picture or something, 
too. Make it good.

00:10:16.170 --> 00:10:18.140
Just give me a holler when you're done.

00:10:18.140 --> 00:10:20.820
I'm counting on you kids.

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:19.510
Make it good?

00:10:19.510 --> 00:10:21.810
That's, like, the worst kind of direction...

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:27.960
Um, Tamaru-kun, are you okay with this? 
He didn't really give you much of a choice.

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:31.840
Nah, I didn't have any plans, so it's fine.

00:10:31.840 --> 00:10:34.460
I see. That's good, then.

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:36.450
Uh, I can't draw, though.

00:10:36.450 --> 00:10:39.050
Oh, that's okay. I'll draw.

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:41.930
Well, let's write the message first, 
and then decorate it and whatnot.

00:10:42.320 --> 00:10:44.990
Tamaru, you write "Graduation Day." 
I'll write "Congratulations."

00:10:44.990 --> 00:10:47.100
Then Ichika writes "everyone."

00:10:47.100 --> 00:10:48.430
Yeah, sure.

00:10:50.060 --> 00:10:53.180
You just need to make your 
letters smaller, Amakusa.

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:53.610
And now

00:10:53.180 --> 00:10:55.950
Actually, I'm pretty sure 
your part is crooked.

00:10:55.950 --> 00:10:57.250
What do you think, Ichika?

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:57.840
Huh?

00:10:58.260 --> 00:10:59.830
Um...

00:11:00.240 --> 00:11:01.550
I can't say.

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:08.350
And by the way, don't think I haven't 
noticed you two acting weird.

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:11.010
You're not speaking as clearly 
as you usually do, Ichika,

00:11:11.010 --> 00:11:13.810
and Tamaru, you're trying not to look at her.

00:11:14.390 --> 00:11:16.860
You're being awkward, and it's 
making everything else awkward.

00:11:20.650 --> 00:11:25.150
Arima... Amakusa knows that I asked you out.

00:11:25.150 --> 00:11:25.660
Huh?

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:27.800
Wait. Rio, you knew?

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:30.390
Well, something seemed to be bothering you,

00:11:31.190 --> 00:11:35.250
so I asked Tamaru if he knew anything 
about that, and he told me.

00:11:35.550 --> 00:11:37.230
Oh...

00:11:37.230 --> 00:11:42.590
And things are awkward right now because 
Arima rejected me the other day.

00:11:43.360 --> 00:11:47.480
I'm not trying to sound bitter or anything. 
I'm just telling her what happened.

00:11:47.480 --> 00:11:49.270
N-No, it's fine.

00:11:50.430 --> 00:11:53.650
I see. So that's what happened.

00:11:53.650 --> 00:11:55.040
Hey, Rio...

00:11:55.890 --> 00:11:59.110
I always talk to you about everything...

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:03.800
but I thought I needed to 
figure this out myself,

00:12:04.440 --> 00:12:05.450
so I didn't tell you.

00:12:08.010 --> 00:12:09.040
I'm sorry.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:13.290
So you were able to come up with 
your own answer and tell Tamaru?

00:12:14.770 --> 00:12:15.210
Yeah.

00:12:17.470 --> 00:12:19.270
Then everything's fine.

00:12:19.270 --> 00:12:20.230
Rio...

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:25.050
It just made me feel kinda lonely 
when you wouldn't tell me,

00:12:25.050 --> 00:12:26.600
so I tried to force you to.

00:12:27.100 --> 00:12:29.850
I might've been a bit bratty. Sorry about that.

00:12:31.030 --> 00:12:31.820
Rio...

00:12:32.510 --> 00:12:33.900
You're so cute.

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.220
Uh, what? That pisses me off somehow.

00:12:36.670 --> 00:12:37.760
Sorry, my bad.

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:42.220
Actually, I think Tamaru's heart 
is hanging on by a thread now.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:45.740
Yeah, just keep pushing that knife deeper.

00:12:45.740 --> 00:12:47.430
I-I'm so sorry, Tamaru-kun!

00:12:47.430 --> 00:12:49.280
It stings even more when you apologize.

00:12:49.280 --> 00:12:51.690
I'm sor— No, wait! I mean—

00:12:52.480 --> 00:12:53.320
I...

00:12:54.000 --> 00:12:59.180
just didn't know how to act around you, 
so this might've been a good chance.

00:12:59.850 --> 00:13:08.310
Next time things get awkward between us, 
let's just laugh and reset a bit, yeah?

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:11.570
I really don't want things 
to be awkward between us.

00:13:12.430 --> 00:13:13.270
Yeah.

00:13:14.310 --> 00:13:15.740
Well, since that's settled...

00:13:16.470 --> 00:13:21.320
Tamaru, hurry up and match the size of 
"Graduation Day" to "Congratulations."

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:23.770
What? Match yours to mine.

00:13:21.320 --> 00:13:25.950
<b>Menacing</b>

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:25.950
You're still going to argue about this?

00:13:25.950 --> 00:13:28.490
You two seem like you've opened up more.

00:13:28.490 --> 00:13:30.600
No, I just know I don't 
need to hold back anymore.

00:13:30.600 --> 00:13:31.550
Yeah.

00:13:33.430 --> 00:13:34.440
Oh?

00:13:34.440 --> 00:13:36.980
What are you three doing here?

00:13:37.460 --> 00:13:39.890
Sacchan, Ru-chan, want to help us?

00:13:39.890 --> 00:13:41.230
Help with what?

00:13:41.230 --> 00:13:45.930
Perfect timing. Let's have them pick 
who should change their font size.

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:54.220
<b>Graduation Day
Congratulations, Everyone</b>

00:14:00.720 --> 00:14:05.470
Hey, this is great! There seems 
to be more of you now, though.

00:14:05.470 --> 00:14:10.220
Are you going to buy us drinks, too,
even though we joined in later?

00:14:10.220 --> 00:14:11.720
B-But of course.

00:14:11.720 --> 00:14:12.840
Yay!

00:14:13.630 --> 00:14:16.290
Next year, it'll be you guys graduating.

00:14:19.410 --> 00:14:23.210
Oh, right. We'll be one step 
closer to being adults.

00:14:24.210 --> 00:14:27.760
Next year, I won't be a high 
school student anymore.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:32.180
I wonder if I'll be more mature by then...

00:14:32.180 --> 00:14:34.710
What? Getting all sentimental, Ichika?

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:36.280
Actually, I might be.

00:14:37.270 --> 00:14:41.530
Arima... You're a year early for that.

00:14:41.530 --> 00:14:43.600
Okay, what do you all want to drink?

00:14:43.600 --> 00:14:44.640
Something fizzy.

00:14:44.640 --> 00:14:45.500
Me, too.

00:14:45.500 --> 00:14:46.490
I'll take coffee.

00:14:46.490 --> 00:14:47.650
I'll have tea.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:49.930
Oh, I'll have some tea, too. Thank you!

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:54.910
Koikimo

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:59.920
Koikimo

00:14:54.910 --> 00:14:59.920
<b>Ryo's Graduation Album</b>

00:14:56.930 --> 00:14:59.920
Hated smiling

00:15:00.350 --> 00:15:02.670
<i>I honestly can't believe it myself.</i>

00:15:03.020 --> 00:15:05.800
<i>To be honest, I really want to deny it...</i>

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:09.550
<i>But the same answer keeps 
circling in my head.</i>

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:12.130
<i>When I think of the word "love" or "like,"</i>

00:15:12.130 --> 00:15:14.140
<i>he's the one who comes to mind...</i>

00:15:15.860 --> 00:15:16.810
Now,

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.100
if you'll look down at your tablet.

00:15:16.810 --> 00:15:19.100
<b>Ichika-san,
\hIn regard to your White Day</b>

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:20.990
Hang on a sec.

00:15:20.990 --> 00:15:21.880
Yes?

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:24.860
You said this was important.

00:15:25.270 --> 00:15:27.980
You seriously can't mean this... do you?

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:29.480
I absolutely do.

00:15:29.480 --> 00:15:30.950
Now, if you'll flip to page 3—

00:15:30.950 --> 00:15:33.270
And why are you starting some presentation?!

00:15:33.770 --> 00:15:36.220
Ichika-san... I've been thinking.

00:15:37.490 --> 00:15:41.480
After receiving such a passionate 
Valentine's Day present from you,

00:15:41.480 --> 00:15:44.220
I need to make your 
White Day just as special!

00:15:44.220 --> 00:15:45.000
Please, no.

00:15:45.000 --> 00:15:47.800
And I tend to do whatever I feel like,

00:15:47.800 --> 00:15:51.210
so I thought it'd be a better idea to give 
you a presentation and get your feedback.

00:15:51.210 --> 00:15:53.420
I'm glad you're realizing your flaws,

00:15:53.420 --> 00:15:56.050
but I'm not your superior or client!

00:15:56.050 --> 00:15:58.980
Ah, so you prefer surprises!

00:15:58.980 --> 00:16:01.110
In that case, we'll need 
this other document...

00:15:59.200 --> 00:16:02.890
Clackity Clackity
Clackity Clackity

00:16:01.110 --> 00:16:03.330
Do you even know what White Day is?

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:06.840
This presentation is canceled! 
Please just listen to me for a sec!

00:16:04.860 --> 00:16:08.270
<i>There's no point in doing a presentation 
if it's supposed to be a surprise, right?</i>

00:16:10.900 --> 00:16:15.880
<i>I do actually like this guy... 
don't I? I think so.</i>

00:16:15.880 --> 00:16:18.280
Why not at least take a look at the document?

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:22.210
I picked up some sweets I figured you'd like.

00:16:22.210 --> 00:16:25.760
<i>Why is this making him look special?</i>

00:16:25.760 --> 00:16:28.290
<i>I'm not sure why, but this is so aggravating.</i>

00:16:29.200 --> 00:16:34.860
<i>Ryo-san does a lot for me, 
despite the awful things I've said to him.</i>

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:40.930
Retrieving my used toothpicks

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:40.930
Waiting for me on my way 
home from school

00:16:35.430 --> 00:16:40.930
He does things that deserve criticism

00:16:35.720 --> 00:16:39.960
<i>Though he can't really blame me, 
considering some of his actions.</i>

00:16:39.960 --> 00:16:45.940
<i>But... am I even able to do 
anything for him in return?</i>

00:16:44.750 --> 00:16:45.940
Ichika-san?

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:50.630
<i>He's ten years older than me. 
I just don't see how we can get along.</i>

00:16:49.460 --> 00:16:50.610
Ichika-san.

00:16:51.400 --> 00:16:55.540
<i>And in the first place, 
do I actually like Ryo-san?</i>

00:16:55.540 --> 00:16:56.280
Ichika-san?

00:16:58.450 --> 00:16:59.810
Are you all right?

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:03.310
Y-Your face! Your face is too close!

00:17:03.310 --> 00:17:05.310
I was worried that you weren't feeling well.

00:17:05.310 --> 00:17:07.710
I was just overwhelmed by all 
your ridiculous documents!

00:17:08.980 --> 00:17:10.420
Perhaps I went too far.

00:17:10.420 --> 00:17:13.160
Well, that's nothing new.

00:17:13.730 --> 00:17:19.800
<i>I'm so frustrated and embarrassed by 
the sudden mood swings he's causing...</i>

00:17:20.430 --> 00:17:21.820
<i>This feels so weird.</i>

00:17:23.620 --> 00:17:25.490
I'm going to get some water.

00:17:25.490 --> 00:17:27.370
I can go get some for you.

00:17:27.370 --> 00:17:30.010
At least let me get my own water.

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:35.110
Matsushima

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:35.110
Matsushima

00:17:31.860 --> 00:17:35.110
Want to go
drinking tonight
around 7 PM?

00:17:32.890 --> 00:17:35.110
<i>Matsushima's inviting me out to drink.</i>

00:17:35.660 --> 00:17:37.740
<i>I don't have any plans, so I guess I'll go.</i>

00:17:38.590 --> 00:17:42.210
Ah, so that's how this works.

00:17:42.210 --> 00:17:43.490
Thank you so much.

00:17:43.490 --> 00:17:44.120
Oh, no problem!

00:17:44.380 --> 00:17:47.310
Please, go right ahead. Would you 
like me to get you some water?

00:17:47.310 --> 00:17:50.200
Oh, what a sweet young girl. Thank you.

00:17:51.090 --> 00:17:53.500
<i>H-He's gently watching over her!</i>

00:17:53.500 --> 00:17:57.130
<i>May your White Day be a success, 
super-hot businessman guy!</i>

00:18:05.870 --> 00:18:06.830
<b>Fidget...</b>

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:08.330
<b>Fidget...</b>

00:18:10.070 --> 00:18:11.060
Matsushima?

00:18:12.640 --> 00:18:14.700
You don't have to be that surprised.

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:15.940
Well, you startled me.

00:18:15.940 --> 00:18:18.410
Sorry about that. Shall we head in?

00:18:18.410 --> 00:18:19.920
S-Sure.

00:18:26.440 --> 00:18:28.530
I didn't realize it was 
just the two of us tonight.

00:18:28.530 --> 00:18:29.120
Huh?

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:32.300
I figured there'd be a group.

00:18:32.300 --> 00:18:36.950
Oh, right. Sorry. I didn't 
mention it'd be just me.

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.490
You'd prefer a group?

00:18:39.490 --> 00:18:41.460
No, this is fine.

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:42.900
I'm glad to hear that.

00:18:43.740 --> 00:18:46.710
So, today, I was...

00:18:46.710 --> 00:18:48.040
Is something on your mind?

00:18:50.160 --> 00:18:51.700
Sorry, I need to run to the restroom.

00:18:51.700 --> 00:18:53.150
Uh, sure.

00:19:01.240 --> 00:19:03.310
<i>I thought I was ready for this...</i>

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:07.000
<i>But I guess asking someone out 
isn't any easier as an adult.</i>

00:19:08.680 --> 00:19:12.300
<i>But if I have even the slightest chance,</i>

00:19:12.300 --> 00:19:14.970
<i>I want him to know how I feel about him.</i>

00:19:16.880 --> 00:19:17.880
I'm back.

00:19:17.880 --> 00:19:20.250
I plated some salad for both of us.

00:19:20.670 --> 00:19:21.660
Thanks.

00:19:25.530 --> 00:19:30.240
The dressing here is great. I think 
berry sauce is the main ingredient.

00:19:30.240 --> 00:19:31.210
Amakusa.

00:19:32.510 --> 00:19:34.760
There's something I want to tell you.

00:19:36.760 --> 00:19:37.820
Do you mind?

00:19:44.150 --> 00:19:49.110
A little while back, 
you mentioned you had a crush.

00:19:49.110 --> 00:19:50.430
Yeah...

00:19:50.430 --> 00:19:53.630
Do you still have a crush on them?

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:55.880
Yeah.

00:19:57.090 --> 00:19:58.140
I see.

00:20:00.550 --> 00:20:05.140
I expected that, but I invited you out tonight 
because I wanted to tell you how I felt.

00:20:05.650 --> 00:20:09.580
Amakusa, I'm in love with you.

00:20:12.100 --> 00:20:14.230
Wow, I actually said it.

00:20:15.420 --> 00:20:18.780
Hey, do you mind if I ask 
you about your crush?

00:20:18.780 --> 00:20:19.420
Huh?

00:20:19.900 --> 00:20:23.240
I want to work on getting you 
to like me, so I want to know.

00:20:23.870 --> 00:20:24.990
No?

00:20:24.990 --> 00:20:28.190
Wow, you just went all 
the way for it, didn't you?

00:20:28.190 --> 00:20:31.460
Well, I told you how I felt, so I figured 
I didn't need to hold back anymore.

00:20:36.330 --> 00:20:40.460
The girl I'm in love with is 
my younger sister's classmate.

00:20:40.460 --> 00:20:46.570
Classmate? Wait, isn't your 
sister in high school?

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:47.640
She is.

00:20:49.000 --> 00:20:50.720
A high school girl...

00:20:50.720 --> 00:20:52.120
Surprised?

00:20:52.120 --> 00:20:58.080
Yeah, I wasn't expecting that. You said 
I reminded you of someone. Is that her?

00:20:58.080 --> 00:20:58.770
Yeah.

00:20:59.430 --> 00:21:02.000
She was the first person to 
actually see through me

00:21:02.000 --> 00:21:04.780
after I'd gotten full of myself for so long.

00:21:06.010 --> 00:21:07.340
I guess she's a good girl.

00:21:07.750 --> 00:21:10.240
Yeah, she's sincere.

00:21:11.100 --> 00:21:15.970
I can tell how much you care for her 
just by the way you talk about her.

00:21:15.970 --> 00:21:16.650
Yeah?

00:21:17.000 --> 00:21:19.000
Did you tell her you love her?

00:21:19.210 --> 00:21:22.510
Well... Yeah, though it's one-sided.

00:21:22.910 --> 00:21:25.480
I want her to know that 
I actually care about her,

00:21:25.480 --> 00:21:27.780
but I just keep striking out.

00:21:30.040 --> 00:21:31.000
Hey...

00:21:31.850 --> 00:21:34.400
I know you can't help that 
you fell in love with her,

00:21:34.400 --> 00:21:37.350
but if you two were actually 
going to start dating,

00:21:37.900 --> 00:21:41.110
wouldn't the age gap make 
it tough for both of you?

00:21:42.010 --> 00:21:47.720
I personally wouldn't want to see the 
person that I love suffer or be sad.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:50.280
Be sad...

00:21:51.120 --> 00:21:56.010
If you do anything to make Ichika sad, 
I won't support you anymore...

00:21:56.490 --> 00:22:00.930
...but just make sure you don't 
do anything to make Arima sad.

00:22:02.480 --> 00:22:03.370
So...

00:22:11.010 --> 00:22:13.960
Couldn't it be me?

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
Next Time

00:23:34.970 --> 00:23:40.250
"Being Prepared to be Hurt"

00:23:36.030 --> 00:23:38.540
Next time, "Being Prepared to be Hurt."
